    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0334" n="322" xml:id="pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-21T15:00:00-03:00">June 21, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>296. For the Under Secretary from Fenwick. Neutrality Committee expects to
                    dispose of current business by the end of next week. Argentine and Mexican
                    members leaving but with the understanding that they will return at call of
                    chairman if important new business arises. Remaining four members can hold
                    sessions under new rules of procedure. No formal recess being taken. Would
                    suggest that invitation to chairman of the Committee to attend coming
                    consultative meeting of Foreign Ministers<anchor n="92" xml:id="d410-f1"/> as
                    observer would be received appreciatively by the Committee. [Fenwick.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
